WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Harambe was not a radical group.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.960
Harambe was a bonding group . . . a support group, maybe.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.880
And it really gave us that feeling of family.

4
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:20.600
Could come, we had a room we could come and play our music, people would bring old furniture, okay, and come and sit.

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.300
But after that there were just ties, we had ties.

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.160
It was also a focal point to . . . If you had to make a statement,

7
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.560
and Leo [Hamilton] or someone had to represent us, we had a focal point.

8
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.880
So it allowed blacks a place to come, which they didn’t have prior to that.

9
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.720
And it was sort of a . . . Let’s just say it was a small NAACP version.
